    {
      "topic": "whole lifecycle",
      "result": "Correct for the measured per-cell boundary: driver.py lines 204-211 begins before prepare and ends after owner finish. consumer_transport.py lines 90-119 and 182-199 include CLI spawn, prompt submission, stream consumption, process/bridge cleanup. Hence whole_s includes backend setup, consumer startup, answer, consumer cleanup and owner close. It excludes earlier one-time build/install/preflight and review, and final CONSUMER.json persistence after the timing sample."
    },
    {
      "topic": "prompt-to-final",
      "result": "Time starts after prompt bytes are submitted and ends at receipt of the final public agent_message event; checked against raw timestamps. It is distinct from whole lifecycle and is not pure provider inference time."
    },
    {
      "topic": "tool overlap",
      "result": "Tool interval union is computed inside consumer wall; sums and union are reported separately and never added again to whole_s. Independent endpoint-sweep matched three raw cells. Tool durations are wrapper/owner measured, not isolated engine CPU."
    },
    {
      "topic": "usage",
      "result": "Inclusive total = input_tokens + output_tokens. cached_input_tokens stays an input subset, reasoning_output_tokens stays an output subset, and uncached input is input minus cached. All 18 rows obey this arithmetic; sample turn.completed events match exactly. cache_write_input_tokens is zero throughout, so no unreviewed cache-write counting extension is needed."
    },
    {
      "topic": "public frames versus other byte counts",
      "result": "95 ID-bearing public requests include 59 tools/call plus 36 control requests; 18 notifications remain separate. Public TX/RX actual JSON frame sizes include directory/handshake traffic; response text UTF-8 payload is separately counted. owner_intended_tool_wire_bytes is separate, not added to actual public traffic. These are recorded public application frames, not TCP headers, provider tokens or all internal RPC bytes."
    },
    {
      "topic": "failed attempts",
      "result": "59 tool attempts include all 3 explicit errors; 53 native and 6 scene-observe attempts. No status-tool call appeared. The failed quality answer remains in the same six-group denominators and timing/token summaries."
    }
